 1. **CI runs `cargo make ci`, the command a contributor runs.** One local command checks what CI checks: formatting, clippy with warnings as errors, the tests with the conformance set, the crates' API docs with no broken intra-doc link (`docs`), the WebAssembly build, cargo-deny, line coverage of at least 99%, and every TypeScript package built, linted and tested. The workflow sets up the tools and calls it; it holds no check of its own, so the two can't drift. Coverage runs the tests, the conformance set's among them, so `ci` doesn't run them a second time; the documentation examples, which coverage leaves out, run on their own (`doctest`). The packages' lint and tests keep their dependency order too: in any order (`--no-sort`) they gained 6 s on the runner's four cores, and tests sensitive to timing failed under the extra load.
